@startuml
title Shadow - Forecasting Prediction Request Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

actor User
component "Predictions tab\n(TASK-057D)" as ui
component "FastAPI prediction API" as api
database "PostgreSQL\nrequests + saved versions" as database
component "Prediction worker supervisor\n(local + release Compose runtime)" as worker
component "One supervised\ncalculation child\n(own process group)" as child
component "CmdStan processes\n(Prophet fit)" as cmdstan
folder "Private per-child\n/tmp directory" as childtmp
component "Organisation States +\nTwin Structure source services" as sources

User --> ui : submit, inspect, cancel
ui --> api : HTTPS request summaries\n(two-second visible polling)
api --> database : freeze snapshot; enqueue;\nrequest/list/cancel state
database --> worker : FIFO claim guarded by\nadvisory lock
worker --> child : detached snapshot
child --> worker : detached complete results
child --> cmdstan : starts in its group
child --> childtmp : TMPDIR / MPLCONFIGDIR
cmdstan --> childtmp : model and output files
worker --> childtmp : creates; removes after reaping
worker --> database : atomic version publication\nand completed state
api --> sources : submission-time read only

note bottom of api
  Submission commits the frozen request before 202.
  Accepted work never depends on browser/session lifetime.
end note

note bottom of child
  No source reads, queue access or publication.
  First action: os.setsid(), then private TMPDIR.
  Supervisor checks cancellation/ownership each second;
  stop sends SIGTERM to the child and process group
  child PID, SIGKILL both after two seconds, and reaps.
  After every outcome: SIGKILL to group child PID
  (missing group ignored), then remove the directory.
end note

note bottom of database
  One global calculation; no broker, retries,
  scheduler, priorities or parallel execution.
end note

note bottom of worker
  Same backend image as API/migration; database-only settings.
  Dedicated health check, automatic restart, init and shutdown grace.
end note
@enduml
